---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { content } from '../lib/content';
const { sources } = await content();
const order = { book: 0, archive: 1, web: 2 } as const;
const list = [...sources].sort((a, b) => order[a.data.kind] - order[b.data.kind]);
---
<Base title="Sources & method" description="The books, archives and methods behind Photography Through Time.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Sources &amp; method</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Each entry lists its own references and, where one is freely available, a primary source: the original paper, patent or manual. Every link is checked to load. Text is written fresh from these sources; nothing is copied from the books.</p>
    <p><strong>Dates.</strong> Most inventions grew over years. Each star sits at a widely used starting point (a first demonstration, a patent, a first product), and where the start is gradual or disputed the entry gives a range. Where sources disagree, the entry says so.</p>
    <p><strong>Impact</strong> ("changed photography for everyone", "major", "significant", "niche") is a judgment for orientation, not a measurement.</p>
    <p><strong>Images</strong> are public domain only, each credited with its source.</p>
    <h2>General sources</h2>
    <ul class="src">{list.map((s) => <li>{s.data.url ? <a href={s.data.url} rel="noopener">{s.data.label} ↗</a> : s.data.label}{s.data.note && <span class="n"> {s.data.note}</span>}</li>)}</ul>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .src { padding-left: 18px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .n { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13.5px; }
</style>
